cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository's mathematical model, simulation code, or generated
  results, please cite this unpublished research project. The complete
  manuscript is currently retained by the author and has not been formally
  published.
type: software
title: >-
  Optimal Stopping Model for VA-ECMO Liberation Based on LVOT VTI Derived
  Latent Physiological Reserve Under Recovery Uncertainty
authors:
  - name: Prihantini
abstract: >-
  Literature-parameterized computational proof-of-concept for model-defined
  VA-ECMO liberation timing. The project combines four nonlinear ordinary
  differential equations, simulated LVOT VTI, a finite-horizon Bellman stopping
  rule, a descriptive four-state continuous-time Markov layer, sensitivity and
  uncertainty analyses, and internal synthetic diagnostics. No patient-level
  calibration or external clinical validation was performed.
keywords:
  - VA-ECMO
  - LVOT VTI
  - optimal stopping
  - nonlinear ordinary differential equations
  - latent physiological reserve
  - uncertainty quantification
  - mathematical modeling
